KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a < b: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ !\(b < a\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no comparison operator
--
cbmc reports "no comparison operator for an operand of class type 'struct
iter'": the hidden friend operator<=> template is not a rewritten candidate
when its return type names T; with std::strong_ordering, or with the
alias template applied to non-dependent arguments, the program verifies.
With libstdc++ 16, std::string::iterator is not random_access_iterator
because of this, span<char> cannot be made from a string, and
_Seq_sink::_M_reserve and _M_span of <format> lose their bodies
(cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_format.desc, broken-libstdcxx16).
Reduced from that with cvise (g++ 16 as the validity check).
